        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2b507c74-edd6-53fa-8228-52d57c47df5c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Hibiscus waimeae, H. arnottianus, Hawaiian hibiscus, Urera kaalae\n- Places: Oʻahu, Molokaʻi, Hawaii\n- Concepts: native species, flower color, habitats, associated plants\n\nFacts:\n- Hawaiian hibiscus are seven species of hibiscus that are regarded as native to Hawaii.\n- H. arnottianus of Oʻahu and Molokaʻi and H. waimeae are the only Hawaiian hibiscuses with white flowers.\n- H. waimeae inhabits coastal mesic, mixed mesic, and wet forests at elevations of 250 meters and above.\n- Urera kaalae is associated with maile (Alyxia oliviformis), hame (Antidesma platyphyllum), Asplenium kaulfusii, Athyrium species, and ʻāwikiwiki (Canavalia species).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
